WEBVTT

00:01:59.366 --> 00:02:03.460
It contains a program designed 
to gain control of a bot

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.815
and give it new instructions.

00:02:05.815 --> 00:02:09.871
But if it’s uploaded to any furnace-
bot other than the original,

00:02:09.871 --> 00:02:12.741
the 0 bot will override 
the instructions

00:02:12.741 --> 00:02:16.365
and destroy the data crystal 
in the process.

00:02:16.365 --> 00:02:18.760
The feeding is just 
a few minutes away,

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:22.319
and there’s only one 
chance to get this right.

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:26.568
Fortunately, Hedge’s ability 
to store data can help.

00:02:26.568 --> 00:02:27.773
In programming,

00:02:27.773 --> 00:02:32.117
a piece of information gets 
stored in something called a variable.